# R11: the Old Pyethymer Place. The mayor has chained its gate; children dare each other in and do not come back; the house moves when not watched. It is a House of
# Horror for a party far stronger than level 3, so this is the gate and the rumour only: the house itself opens in a later pass.

~ gate
Narrator: A chain and a padlock hold the gate, and a board nailed across it says BY ORDER OF THE MAYOR. On the step behind lies one small child's shoe, laces still tied.
Narrator: The house leans over a lane of empty ones. When you look at its windows, it seems to have been looking at you a moment before.
quest the_pyethymer_place rumour
* Ask what folk say about the house -> ask
* [Athletics DC 15] Try the chain -> chain_ok | chain_fail
* Leave it -> END

~ ask
Narrator: Nobody who lives on the lane will say it plainly. A woman at her gate says the children dare each other, a boy at the inn says the house has more rooms inside than it has outside, and everyone says the shoe belongs to somebody.
-> gate

~ chain_ok
Narrator: The padlock gives with a dull crack. The gate swings an inch, and something in the house breathes in, long and slow.
Narrator: The shoe on the step is gone. Behind you, in the lane, a child laughs, and nobody is there. You pull the gate shut and press the chain back round it, and it feels like the right thing to have done.
quest the_pyethymer_place chained
-> END

~ chain_fail
Narrator: The chain does not budge, and the house seems to settle a little, pleased.
quest the_pyethymer_place chained
-> END
